1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:02,133
A mango from the tree.

2
00:00:02,133 --> 00:00:03,398
A bowl of curd.

3
00:00:03,398 --> 00:00:04,550
Your own hand.

4
00:00:04,950 --> 00:00:06,480
They look nothing alike.

5
00:00:06,480 --> 00:00:08,906
But all three are full of living cells.

6
00:00:09,356 --> 00:00:11,365
Diya noticed this in her kitchen.

7
00:00:11,365 --> 00:00:15,856
She wants to be a doctor, so she asked:
what is this subject really about?

8
00:00:16,206 --> 00:00:20,486
In NEET, ninety of the one hundred
and eighty questions are biology.

9
00:00:20,486 --> 00:00:21,616
Half the paper.

10
00:00:22,116 --> 00:00:26,552
By the end, you will know what biology
studies, how life is organised,

11
00:00:26,552 --> 00:00:28,669
and the map of everything ahead.

12
00:00:29,319 --> 00:00:30,901
So what is biology?

13
00:00:31,251 --> 00:00:32,574
Bio means life.

14
00:00:32,574 --> 00:00:34,009
Logy means study.

15
00:00:34,009 --> 00:00:36,889
Biology is the study of living things.

16
00:00:37,339 --> 00:00:39,092
Botany studies plants.

17
00:00:39,092 --> 00:00:40,960
Zoology studies animals.

18
00:00:40,960 --> 00:00:44,592
Microbiology studies
microbes, too small to see.

19
00:00:44,992 --> 00:00:47,131
Physiology asks how bodies work.

20
00:00:47,131 --> 00:00:50,494
Genetics, how traits pass
from parents to children.

21
00:00:50,494 --> 00:00:53,449
Ecology, how living
things share the planet.

22
00:00:54,099 --> 00:00:57,660
Now let's zoom into one mango
leaf, one level at a time.

23
00:00:58,010 --> 00:00:59,600
The leaf is an organ.

24
00:00:59,600 --> 00:01:02,821
It has one main job:
making food from sunlight.

25
00:01:03,321 --> 00:01:04,221
Zoom in.

26
00:01:04,093 --> 00:01:09,095
The leaf is made of tissues: groups of
similar cells doing one job together.

27
00:01:09,595 --> 00:01:10,591
Zoom again.

28
00:01:10,591 --> 00:01:16,079
One cell, with its cell wall, nucleus,
large vacuole and green chloroplasts.

29
00:01:16,579 --> 00:01:18,312
Zoom into one chloroplast.

30
00:01:18,312 --> 00:01:20,646
This organelle is the cell's kitchen.

31
00:01:20,646 --> 00:01:22,786
Here, the cell makes its food.

32
00:01:23,286 --> 00:01:26,473
Inside it, chlorophyll
molecules catch the sunlight.

33
00:01:26,473 --> 00:01:28,317
Molecules are made of atoms.

34
00:01:28,317 --> 00:01:30,510
That is the bottom of the ladder.

35
00:01:31,160 --> 00:01:34,968
Let's write the full ladder, from
small to big, one step at a time.

36
00:01:35,318 --> 00:01:36,218
Step one.

37
00:01:36,172 --> 00:01:40,596
Molecules build organelles, the
small working parts inside a cell.

38
00:01:41,346 --> 00:01:42,246
Step two.

39
00:01:42,110 --> 00:01:45,169
Organelles work together,
and make a living cell.

40
00:01:45,919 --> 00:01:46,869
Step three.

41
00:01:46,869 --> 00:01:48,881
Similar cells form a tissue.

42
00:01:48,881 --> 00:01:51,637
Different tissues join to form an organ.

43
00:01:52,387 --> 00:01:53,347
Step four.

44
00:01:53,347 --> 00:01:56,743
Organs that work together
form an organ system.

45
00:01:56,743 --> 00:01:59,676
Organ systems together make one organism.

46
00:02:00,426 --> 00:02:01,374
Step five.

47
00:02:01,374 --> 00:02:04,286
One kind of organism forms a population.

48
00:02:04,286 --> 00:02:06,402
Populations form a community.

49
00:02:06,402 --> 00:02:09,924
A community with its
surroundings is an ecosystem.

50
00:02:10,674 --> 00:02:11,686
Remember this.

51
00:02:11,686 --> 00:02:14,514
The cell is the smallest
unit that is alive.

52
00:02:15,114 --> 00:02:17,498
That idea is called the cell theory.

53
00:02:17,848 --> 00:02:21,423
In eighteen thirty eight, Schleiden
found plants made of cells.

54
00:02:21,423 --> 00:02:24,292
A year later, Schwann
found the same in animals.

55
00:02:24,742 --> 00:02:29,473
In eighteen fifty five, Virchow added
the last piece: new cells come only

56
00:02:29,473 --> 00:02:31,545
from cells that already exist.

57
00:02:31,995 --> 00:02:36,367
So today we say: all living things are
made of cells, and every cell comes

58
00:02:36,367 --> 00:02:37,565
from another cell.

59
00:02:38,215 --> 00:02:40,604
Some living things are just one cell.

60
00:02:40,604 --> 00:02:42,499
Others are made of trillions.

61
00:02:42,849 --> 00:02:44,559
An amoeba is one cell.

62
00:02:44,559 --> 00:02:48,008
That single cell eats,
moves, grows and divides.

63
00:02:48,008 --> 00:02:49,872
It is the whole organism.

64
00:02:50,322 --> 00:02:52,756
You are many cells sharing the work.

65
00:02:52,756 --> 00:02:57,260
Muscle cells move you, nerve cells
carry messages, red blood cells carry

66
00:02:57,260 --> 00:02:58,160
oxygen.

67
00:02:58,510 --> 00:02:59,422
Your turn.

68
00:02:59,422 --> 00:03:01,520
Yeast makes bread dough rise.

69
00:03:01,520 --> 00:03:03,523
Is yeast one cell or many?

70
00:03:03,523 --> 00:03:04,865
Pause and decide.

71
00:03:08,065 --> 00:03:08,965
One cell!

72
00:03:08,928 --> 00:03:11,864
Yeast is a fungus made of a single cell.

73
00:03:11,864 --> 00:03:14,032
That one cell does every job.

74
00:03:14,683 --> 00:03:17,976
Why does biology sort
living things into groups?

75
00:03:17,976 --> 00:03:22,679
Scientists have described about one
point seven to one point eight million

76
00:03:22,679 --> 00:03:23,579
kinds.

77
00:03:23,771 --> 00:03:25,764
No one can remember them all.

78
00:03:25,764 --> 00:03:30,496
So we sort them, from big groups called
kingdoms down to a single species.

79
00:03:30,946 --> 00:03:35,666
And each species gets one scientific
name, used all over the world.

80
00:03:35,666 --> 00:03:37,856
The mango is Mangifera indica.

81
00:03:37,856 --> 00:03:39,447
We are Homo sapiens.

82
00:03:40,097 --> 00:03:42,757
Here is the map of PUC biology.

83
00:03:43,107 --> 00:03:47,501
First year: the variety of life, the
structure of plants and animals, the

84
00:03:47,501 --> 00:03:50,856
cell, how plants work, and
how the human body works.

85
00:03:51,306 --> 00:03:56,716
Second year: reproduction, genetics and
evolution, biology in human welfare,

86
00:03:56,716 --> 00:03:58,813
biotechnology, and ecology.

87
00:03:59,263 --> 00:04:04,145
Every lesson here starts with something
you notice, builds a labelled diagram,

88
00:04:04,145 --> 00:04:07,283
runs the process, and
ends with exam practice.

89
00:04:07,933 --> 00:04:09,462
Now, a worked example.

90
00:04:09,462 --> 00:04:11,695
Let's place six things on the ladder.

91
00:04:12,045 --> 00:04:13,966
Haemoglobin is a molecule.

92
00:04:13,966 --> 00:04:16,725
It is the protein that carries oxygen.

93
00:04:17,175 --> 00:04:19,426
A mitochondrion is an organelle.

94
00:04:19,426 --> 00:04:21,741
It releases energy for the cell.

95
00:04:22,191 --> 00:04:23,902
A red blood cell is a cell.

96
00:04:24,352 --> 00:04:26,739
Blood is a tissue, a liquid tissue.

97
00:04:26,739 --> 00:04:30,784
Its cells and fluid work together
to carry things around the body.

98
00:04:31,284 --> 00:04:32,884
The heart is an organ.

99
00:04:32,884 --> 00:04:37,218
With the blood vessels and the blood,
it forms the circulatory system,

100
00:04:37,218 --> 00:04:38,411
an organ system.

101
00:04:39,061 --> 00:04:40,527
Now, the exam trap.

102
00:04:40,877 --> 00:04:44,914
Many students say the cell is the
smallest level of organisation.

103
00:04:45,314 --> 00:04:49,797
But cells are made of organelles,
and organelles are made of molecules.

104
00:04:49,797 --> 00:04:53,844
The cell is the smallest unit
of life, not the smallest level.

105
00:04:54,494 --> 00:04:55,915
Where is this asked?

106
00:04:55,915 --> 00:05:00,434
As one line statements: which level
comes next, or what is the basic unit

107
00:05:00,434 --> 00:05:01,334
of life.

108
00:05:01,769 --> 00:05:02,987
Exam level now.

109
00:05:02,987 --> 00:05:04,783
Read the four statements.

110
00:05:04,783 --> 00:05:06,476
Which ones are correct?

111
00:05:06,476 --> 00:05:07,746
Pause and solve.

112
00:05:13,146 --> 00:05:14,408
The answer is A.

113
00:05:14,408 --> 00:05:16,560
Statements one, three and four.

114
00:05:17,060 --> 00:05:18,200
Two is wrong.

115
00:05:18,200 --> 00:05:22,866
Amoeba and yeast are single cells,
yet each is a complete organism.

116
00:05:23,366 --> 00:05:25,594
One and three are the cell theory.

117
00:05:25,594 --> 00:05:27,727
Four is the meaning of a tissue.

118
00:05:28,327 --> 00:05:29,790
Here is your recap.

119
00:05:29,790 --> 00:05:31,292
Screenshot this card.

120
00:05:34,492 --> 00:05:37,329
Can you answer these three
questions without help?

121
00:05:37,729 --> 00:05:38,629
One.

122
00:05:38,204 --> 00:05:40,698
What comes between a cell and an organ?

123
00:05:41,598 --> 00:05:42,498
Two.

124
00:05:42,105 --> 00:05:44,153
Why is blood called a tissue?

125
00:05:45,053 --> 00:05:45,953
Three.

126
00:05:45,707 --> 00:05:48,795
Why is a single amoeba
a complete organism?

127
00:05:49,895 --> 00:05:54,055
Next time: a sugar crystal
grows, and a seed sits still.

128
00:05:54,055 --> 00:05:55,586
Which one is alive?

129
00:05:55,586 --> 00:05:59,076
We find out in characteristics
of living organisms.
